# In the Bleak Midwinter, arranged by DeepSeek Flash and SZ. A slow music-box carol over an open pad and a heartbeat kick, ending in a long fade.
title: In the Bleak Midwinter
composer: Gustav Holst
arranger: DeepSeek Flash & SZ
about: Christina Rossetti wrote the words in 1872 for Scribner's Monthly, a Christmas poem full of frost and stillness. Gustav Holst set it as the hymn tune Cranham in 1906, named after the Gloucestershire village where he was born; Harold Darke's later setting is the one often sung by choirs.
year: 1906
source: public-domain
category: carols
key: F major
style: ambient
tempo: 72
time: 4/4

